<header><p class="st-kicker">tribal confederation · Egypt, North Africa and Sudan</p><h1 class="st-title">Austuriani</h1><p class="st-meta">360 CE – 450 CE (approx.)</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A Libyan desert people whose raids on Tripolitania and Cyrenaica in the late 4th and 5th centuries exposed Roman weakness.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The Austuriani (Austoriani) are known only from Roman writers. They lived in the desert hinterland of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gulf-of-sirte">Gulf of Sirte</a> and first appear in the 360s, when they raided the territory of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/leptis-magna">Leptis Magna</a> after one of their men, Stachao, was burned alive by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-empire">Romans</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>They were <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/camel">camel</a>-using pastoral tribes without a known central government. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ammianus-marcellinus">Ammianus Marcellinus</a> describes their raids of 363 to 365, which devastated the farms around <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/leptis-magna">Leptis</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tripoli">Oea</a>, and the failure of the military count <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/romanus-comes-africae">Romanus</a>, who demanded supplies and camels before acting. In the early 5th century they raided <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cyrenaica">Cyrenaica</a> repeatedly, as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/synesius">Bishop Synesius of Ptolemais</a> reports in his letters.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>After the mid-5th century the name disappears. They were probably absorbed into, or renamed as, the larger <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/laguatan">Laguatan</a> confederation, which continued to press on <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/tripolitania">Tripolitania</a> and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/praetorian-prefecture-of-africa">Byzantine Africa</a>.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="tribal confederation, 360 CE – 450 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><ellipse cx="44" cy="56" rx="16" ry="24"/><path d="M44 34 V78"/><path d="M68 20 V84"/><path d="M68 20 L63 30 H73 Z"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">tribal confederation</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Egypt, North Africa and Sudan</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:66.87%;width:1.79%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>360 CE – 450 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/4th-century">4th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/5th-century">5th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>tribal confederation</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>nomadic</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Berber religion</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Berber (Libyco-Berber)</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/libya">Libya</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Austoriani</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=405&amp;focus=austuriani" aria-label="Austuriani on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5155 1200 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Austuriani lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5475 1456h0"/><path class="map-dot-ap" d="M5475 1456h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>Location approximate: shown in present-day Libya. <a href="/atlas?year=405&amp;focus=austuriani">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

